Z||000000||zeusrekning||12-04-2000||06:37 PM||||The coupe i just bought is white and has a lot of minor body damage.<BR>Little things like small cracks, bad paint,<BR>where the hood and front facia meet is messed up.<BR>I can't afford a kit car now.<BR>So should i just find replacement panels or buy some fiberglass and let me imagination go at it.<BR>This car is not my daily drive, just my toy.||||reg||1
Z||000001||hugh||12-04-2000||06:45 PM||||Experiment,you may find that you are good at custom work and like it.Let your imagination go.||||reg||1
Z||000002||zeusrekning||12-04-2000||07:15 PM||||ok<BR>i'm all up for it give me ideas or o\pics of what some one would like to see.<BR>If i can do it great if i can't<BR>hell i belive anyone can do almost anything.<BR>What do the fiero owners want to see?<BR>Start with front facia and move rear.<BR>Forgot something<BR>have to research.<BR>How do you make molds<BR>where can i get info on this?<BR>this is the only thing i don't understan.<BR>why does the fiberglass not stick to the mold?<BR><p>[This message has been edited by zeusrekning (edited 12-04-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||hugh||12-04-2000||08:17 PM||||Why make a mold?do it freehand.The fiberglas doesn't stick to the mold if you use butter or oil to wipe it down,and then sprinkle flour all over it. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||zeusrekning||12-04-2000||09:09 PM||||I was thinking i need a mold to get the look I want to start with, then go from there. Cause that fiberglass mat is floppy.<BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||RedOktober||12-04-2000||09:22 PM||||I suggest you find a fiberglass shop or a boat in your area and get some eurothane(sp?) foam blocks and carve out any desired shape. Lay fiblerglass over it, and when it cures, knock out the foam underneath. Do not use the cheap styro foam, it will disolve as soon as the resin hits it.<BR>The fiberglass shop will have everything for you including mold releasers and other stuff to make your life easier.<BR>Hope this helps.<BR><P>------------------<BR>86 SE V6 Auto Turbo Going 3.4 OHV "Red Oktober"<BR>86 2M4 5sp (Beater) "Blackie"<BR>87 GT "Blue Flame"||||reg||1
Z||000006||hugh||12-04-2000||09:25 PM||||I was being a smart ass and you completly ignored me.Seriously,I did some fiberglas work a long time ago on a 1963 Falcon Sprint conv.I removed the bumper and molded a new front end over screening I bought at a hardware store.I did the imperfections in the finish with body filler.It turned out well enough that I painted the car when I was finished and it looked good.||||reg||1
